#. y1:english="\nHello.||Sir,{PA:10} what would you like to drink?\n\n\nYou look drunk.||I don't think you should drink anymore.\nWould you like another drink?\nOh, {PA:10}ok.{PA:20}||Have a nice day!\n\n\nYamazaki 12 Years...\nThis is a very fine whisky.\nThis whisky made its debut in 1984||as the first Japanese pure malt whisky.\nIt was made to commemorate the 60th||anniversary of the Yamazaki distillery,\nwhere the first Japanese whisky||was created.\nYou can say that this represents Yamazaki.\nAs for the taste, it has a mellow yet||powerful flavour characteristic of Yamazaki.\nIt has earned quite a reputation||overseas as well as domestically.\n\n\n\nHakushu 10 Years...\nYour standard Japanese whisky.\nIt's created in the Hakushu distillery||in Kaikomagadake,\nwhich is in the Japanese Alps.\nThe water from that region is very pure.\nPersonally, I like drinking Hakushu\nwhile eating a little tofu...\nAnyways, I recommend Japanese side||dishes to accompany this fine drink.\n\n\n\nSuntory Old Whisky...\nEven someone who doesn't drink has||surely come across one of these bottles\nat one point in time.\nIt's famous for its thick, but mild taste.\nIt came out in 1950 and||for the past 55 years,\nits flavour has attracted many whisky||fans to this charming drink.\n\n\n\nEarly Times...\nA world renown bourbon.\nIt has the unique American edge||and a gorgeous flavour.\nIt's very reasonably priced and||quite enjoyable.\n\n\n\nSuntory Brandy X.O Deluxe...\nThis brandy is made 100% from grapes.\nIt has a thick mature flavor that's suitable||to drink straight or with tonic.\nI'm sure you'll enjoy its refreshing taste.\nThis liquor is very well-balanced.\nThe taste lingers longer||than Suntory Brandy X.O.\n\n\n\nSuntory Brandy V.S.O.P...\nThis is the highest quality brandy in Japan.\nV.S.O.P stands for Very,||Superior, Old and Pale.\nWith 4 kinds of fruity raw spirits||and distinct spirits blended,\nit has a very rich flavour.\n\n\n\nSuntory Brandy V.O...\nThis brandy has a very||smooth and fruity taste.\nIt's reasonably priced and easy to drink,\nwith a taste you won't get tired of anytime||soon. A brandy suitable for beginners.\nEnjoy the unique sweetness of this brandy.\n\n\n\nSuntory Malt's Beer...\nA draft beer put out by Suntory. The makers||of this brew focus not only on the quality\nof the materials like hops but the quality||of water as well. 4 types of natural\nspring water have been carefully||selected for the crafting of this beer.\nNo other draft beers can beat||the aftertaste of Suntory Malt's Beer.\n\n\n\nKyogetsu Green...\nA notable Korean spirit.\nMineral water from Mt. Sorak and||select Korean hops are used to\nproduce a mild taste.\nReasonably priced, this is a fine drink||well-suited for anyone's palette.\n"
